{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437886-beat-generating-merits-gifts-rites-etc","id":437886,"title":"Beat Generating Merits, Gifts, Rites, etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T19:09:44-07:00","id":437886,"title":"Beat Generating Merits, Gifts, Rites, etc.","content":"There seems to be a lot of potential for cooperative generation of beats (especially with Pack Beats p. 85). Unfortunately, merits and gifts aren't sorted and tagged in a searchable filterable database. :-( And I thought we were living in the future. :-D<br /> <br /> Naja... let's make a list! Just the name and page. Copyright and all that.<br /> <br /> Creative Tactician, page 105<br /> Song in Your Heart, page 107<br /> <br /> ... well, that's all I found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:43:35-07:00","id":438239,"title":"","content":"Best combo I can see at the moment for generating lots of beats is,<br /> <br /> Merit, <i>Trained Observer</i> at 3 dots \u2013 8 again on all Perception rolls<br /> <br /> Gift of Hunting Cunning Facet, <i>Honed Senses</i> \u2013 Exceptional Success on 3 success rather than 5.<br /> <br /> Then as optional garnish, Gift of Hunting Wisdom Facet, <i>Impossible Spoor</i> \u2013 2 Auto success on Tracking rolls.<br /> <br /> The single most likely roll that you will be making multiple times in a session is a perception roll. Werewolves get natural bonuses to perception naturally, so anything you can do to boost perception further will increase your chances of exceptional successes and thus increase the number of beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2354,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2354-mremann","user":"mremann","date":". 03-12-2015, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2354-mremann","name":"mremann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T05:58:46-07:00","id":438305,"title":"","content":"Don't forget being Inspired by Song In Your Heart - After hearing a story about hunting and tracking!<br /> While on a Sacred Hunt for... anything and everything you have the time to sacred hunt!<br /> <br /> Trained Observer + Honed Senses + Impossible Spoor + Song In Your Heart (someone else) + Siskur-Dah = Beat Factory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:46:31-07:00","id":438334,"title":"","content":"Another sort of beat factory is trying enough things that your group isn't good at that everyone fails at least one roll every scene. Tack on a policy of always accepting dramatic failures and your Beats will be coming at a super-fast pace. Then whatever gifts and rites and merits you have that can get you out of the crap-storms that ensue will more-or-less be things that grant Beats.<br /> This way, Beats even get to keep their value as units of drama. By making lots and lots and lots of drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:00:36-07:00","id":438484,"title":"","content":"The beat for turning a failure into a dramatic one is once per Chapter (or game session) IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:41:19-07:00","id":438582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437886-beat-generating-merits-gifts-rites-etc?p=438484#post438484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beat for turning a failure into a dramatic one is once per Chapter (or game session) IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once per scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:44:56-07:00","id":438678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437886-beat-generating-merits-gifts-rites-etc?p=438582#post438582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot; Once per scene, when you fail a roll, you may opt to make it a dramatic failure and take a Beat.&quot; - copied from page 85<br /> &quot;Once per scene, if you fail a roll, you may opt to take a Dramatic Failure instead. If you do so, take a Beat. Certain Conditions can have you take an automatic failure as part of their resolutions; you may make these failures Dramatic and take two Beats.&quot; - is how it's put in the GMC book on page 158. I just thought to look there to see if it was per chapter in those rules, so I haven't doubled checked WtF2E to see if there are any such conditions in it. Maybe there are, or maybe the ones referenced here are applicable.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Vampire 2E. Does it say scene or session?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:19:36-07:00","id":438706,"title":"","content":"'Any time you fail a roll, you may opt to make it a dramatic failure and take a Beat. ' From Blood and Smoke. They may have cleaned that up in the other edition.<br /> <br /> Checked, nope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-12-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:24:26-07:00","id":438713,"title":"","content":"Geez... Beat hunters need only make unskilled mental rolls as vampires...<br /> &quot;Oh yes, this is definitely the occult symbol we're looking for&quot;<br /> &quot;No a truck needs its carborator under the... um... back section&quot;<br /> &quot;Doctor, I think you'll find that...&quot;<br /> BAM! I'm an ancient already!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:30:04-07:00","id":438719,"title":"","content":"Dramatic Failures are meant to have dramatic results. It's going to be the Storyteller's decision whether the player can make that decision at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:47:19-07:00","id":438738,"title":"","content":"I get that. And I was being a little flippant about there not being a limit on how often you can do it in vampire.<br /> This thread was started with the intent of getting Beats through carefully crafting situations to grant dramatic success. I'm just saying that there's another side to this coin. <br /> Dramatic Failures as a road to XP means that you're taking the exciting, break-neck speed story where the problems are flying at you left and right. It's crazy, and the Storyteller might not want to try keeping up and has every right to shut you down. But as Experiences are meant to be awarded because player and character had a distinctly dramatic experience, it seems a reasable way to speed up the beats, both mechanical Beats and heartbeats.<br /> If you've got the character-side skills and player-side fortitude to deal with the fallout, this could be a fun option...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:54:49-07:00","id":438742,"title":"","content":"Do you want vampire merits? There are some abilities in vampire 2e.<br /> <br /> Also you missed the Wolf-Blooded tells. Evil Eye gives its victim a beat, because it causes an automatic dramatic failure. And with Tongues the character can roll and fail, then take a dramatic failure for doing acts that normally wouldn't require it, for instance speaking or singing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T13:04:52-07:00","id":438836,"title":"","content":"Another option is to buy your GM a set of Overly Specific Condition Cards, and then make sure your character gets an Extensive Collection of Conditions. Then nearly anything he does will be a failure. The card even specifically says that you can choose to make them dramatic and take extra Beats.<br /> Best of all, when you finally do decide to resolve that one, you get a whole Experience for resolving five conditions at once!<br /> This is really taking things to the realm of silly, though. Those cards came out on April 1st for a reason...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}